throughout the russian revolution many  of you will know that the bolsheviks  weren't the only communist group  involved  in fact another group the mensheviks had  a major part to play in for much of 1917  they stood firmly opposed to the  bolsheviks in many ways  yet as you'll know it was the bolsheviks  who ran russia in the wake of the  revolution and not the mensheviks which  raises the obvious question  why why did the mensheviks lose out to  the bolsheviks  so to begin it's important to note that  the two used to be part of the same  political party the russian social  democratic labour party  after some small ideological  disagreements in 1903 this party broke  into two parts  the first led by vladimir lenin was the  bolsheviks meaning majority  the second led by julius martov was the  mensheviks meaning minority  when world war one broke out in 1914 the  mensheviks and the bolsheviks were both  firmly opposed and when public opinion  started to turn against the war and the  tsar both smelled an opportunity  when the romanovs were ousted and the  february revolution was completed russia  had a brand new government  well actually it had two the provisional  government which had the support of the  remaining russian state and its old  allies  and the petrograd soviet which was a  rival government made up of the  mensheviks the bolsheviks and many of  the socialist revolutionaries  and side note for about a month both of  these governments were housed in the  same building  which must have been quite awkward given  that the coming revolution was just down  the hall to the left  at first the petrograd soviet was  dominated by the mensheviks for the most  part they believed that the best course  forward in order to establish  a communist state was to support the  provisional government because they felt  that russia's economy wasn't  sufficiently developed enough to make  the leap to communism and instead it  needed to go through the industrial  capitalism bit first  whereas the bolsheviks had very  different ideas on how to achieve  a communist state in the end the  mensheviks even ended up taking cabinet  positions and most notably supported the  continuation of russia's involvement in  world war one  and this was a fatal mistake since the  basis of authority for the mensheviks  within the provisional government was  the support  of the soldiery this led to a breakdown  in cooperation between the bolsheviks  and the mensheviks and importantly saw  the bolsheviks rapidly gain support  in july some of their supporters  attempted to overthrow the government  which failed and as a result the  provisional government including the  mensheviks cracked down on the  bolsheviks  leading to the arrest of summon forcing  lenin into exile  it wasn't long afterwards that there was  an attempted military coup which failed  but most people saw the government as  complicit in it  as such many people now turn to the  bolsheviks and things got even more  tense  leading to lenin returning because it  was time for revolution number two  as you'll know this one saw the  bolsheviks placed in complete control  providing you ignored the long and  incredibly brutal civil war that  followed  as the war progressed the bolsheviks who  were now calling themselves the  communist party centralized power and  removed the mensheviks and other  leftists from government positions  this expulsion didn't mean the end of  the mensheviks though  as a result many went south to georgia  and briefly round the country until it  was conquered by the reds in 1921  and in the same year a group of  disenfranchised sailors on the island of  kronstadt just here launched a rebellion  against the government  it was mostly an anarchist one but there  were some left-wing sympathies amongst  the rebels and so after crushing the  revolt the communists promptly used it  as an excuse to ban all other competing  parties in the country  menshevism had finally lost out to  bolshevism  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons james bissonette  sam kelly moneymaker the pastry section  danny maloney  moe marvin cassell rob waterhouse james  castaneda jordan longley spinning three  plates gustav swann jerry lamdin rasheed  ali marcus asner izzy  maggie paxkowski cooling castleman david  silverman coppertone anthony beckett  matthew shipley  lexy schwinn robert wetzel skye  chappelle winston cayward aaron the  white spencer lightfoot and fobo joe
 

